<http://data.silknow.org/event/e2757b4c-37a2-310a-b302-686334860255>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Associated with the wedding of Elizabeth Wroughton Richards to the Reverend Andrew Nugee on 8th August 1854 at Farlington, Hampshire, very probably at St Andrew's..\n\nElizabeth Wroughton Richards (1820?-2/11/1877) was the daughter of Revd. Edward Tew Richards, Rector of Farlington (the next door parish to Wymering). The Richards were Rectors from 1782 to 1925. Following her husband's death, she went on to marry a Dr. Field in 1867, and died 10 years later.\n\nAndrew Nugée (b.31/10/1813 - d.25/12/1858) was the 2nd son of Francis James Nugée who came from a family of Huguenot tailors who emigrated from Bordeaux to Cork between 1748-1752. They made a name for themselves with \"Nugee's waistcoats\" in the early 19th century. He was at Brasenose College, and became a curate in Lambeth prior to becoming Vicar of Wymering in 1851. The living was purchased by his father in the 1840s with a view to presenting his son as Vicar when the next vacancy should occur."@en ;
        ecrm:P14_carried_out_by        <http://data.silknow.org/actor/224d8d70-0244-3f4f-b50a-5c415aa6d240> ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P23_transferred_title_from
                "Given by Edward Nugée QC" ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/b108e894-329c-35af-b3ce-033cedd47d14> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Associated with the wedding of Elizabeth Wroughton Richards to the Reverend Andrew Nugee on 8th August 1854 at Farlington, Hampshire, very probably at St Andrew's..\n\nElizabeth Wroughton Richards (1820?-2/11/1877) was the daughter of Revd. Edward Tew Richards, Rector of Farlington (the next door parish to Wymering). The Richards were Rectors from 1782 to 1925. Following her husband's death, she went on to marry a Dr. Field in 1867, and died 10 years later.\n\nAndrew Nugée (b.31/10/1813 - d.25/12/1858) was the 2nd son of Francis James Nugée who came from a family of Huguenot tailors who emigrated from Bordeaux to Cork between 1748-1752. They made a name for themselves with \"Nugee's waistcoats\" in the early 19th century. He was at Brasenose College, and became a curate in Lambeth prior to becoming Vicar of Wymering in 1851. The living was purchased by his father in the 1840s with a view to presenting his son as Vicar when the next vacancy should occur."@en .

